title: Garp_Gift_Hunt_intro
location: town
---

What a lovely winter day — crisp blue skies, and the cadets have been hard at work clearing snow away from the streets (and the rooftops, too!). It feels great to wander the streets on your day off... until suddenly, you hear a lot of commotion coming from the central plaza.
Rounding the corner, you see that the main thoroughfare is packed with people and merchant stalls hawking wares. What is all this? A banner overhead answers your question: END OF YEAR SELLOUT
Oh. That's right, the end of the year holidays are coming up... and New Years. A certain someone crosses your mind... will you perhaps achieve your goal of being kissed at midnight on New Years Eve? A woman rushes by with brightly colored wrapped gifts and something occurs to you. A gift. You should give them a gift! Can't hurt, certainly (hopefully...)!
And where else to search for a gift but here, at this conveniently timed market?
First though, who the heck are you shopping for?
-character selection- //HOW DO??
<<jump Garp_Gift_Hunt_START>>
===

title: Garp_Gift_Hunt_START
location: town
---

You let your feet wander, trying to think of a good gift for Garp. When you think of him, your mind always goes back to the fact that he's a living legend. He's the Hero of the Marines, his protege is the next rising star of the Navy, and the stories of his exploits are absolutely mind-boggling no matter how often you hear them. You can't help but wonder which parts of his legacy he cares the most about, or even how he feels about some of his stories.
Suddenly, a stall catches your attention. A shorter man with pince-nez glasses, a newsboy cap, and an olive green button-down shirt is arranging some merchandise. From the look of it, there's old, framed News Coo articles, along with some framed pictures depicting famous events. Your eyes widen. These could be perfect!
You walk over to the stall, and the man, clearly the owner, looks over to you with a wide smile. Two old-looking lamps illuminate the stall, while crates of framed pictures and documents are set up to entice curious customers to thumb through what's on offer.
Owner: Ah, hello hello! Here for a copy of the best news that's been approved to print?
{$name}: Um, yeah! Or... Maybe? I don't know. What do you have?
Owner: Well, well, I'm glad you asked! I've got loads of old News Coo printings! And if you aren't one for news, these pictures tell a thousand words!
Owner: Anything you're looking for? Or maybe a certain time or event? Heck, even a particular person in mind?
{$name}: Let me think...
-> Do you have anything related to Garp the Fist?
    <<jump Garp_Gift_Hunt_good_gift>>
-> Do you have anything related to Gold Roger?
    <<jump Garp_Gift_Hunt_bad_gift>>
===

title: Garp_Gift_Hunt_good_gift
location: town
---

Owner: Ah, a Hero of the Marines fan, are ya? Well, I've got something that will suit your fancy.
The owner goes over to a particular crate and looks through the framed items. After a while, he pulls out a certain piece and brings it over to an easel to display for you.
The picture is the first thing to grab your attention. If you didn't know him as well as you do, you might not have recognized him immediately, but one of the figures in the picture is most assuredly Monkey D. Garp. The giant smile on his face (and the scar by his eye) are clear giveaways.
Next to him is a gorgeous woman that looks vaguely like Kujaku, and it takes you a moment to realize that this could only be Tsuru.
Then there's a third person who must be Sengoku, and he looks so serious, like he's upset that he's posing for a picture instead of punishing evil or whatever.
The article appears to be an interview. You smile at some of their responses.
“Garp-san, what are your plans for the future?”
“Hell if I know! Eat rice cakes and beat up pirates, I guess!”
You can't help but chuckle. That sounds just like him; despite everything he's been through, who he is at heart hasn't changed much.
You turn to the stall owner, who's staring at you with an expectant expression.
-> I'll take this one!
    <<jump Garp_Gift_Hunt_gift_wrapup>>
-> [If PC has not done ::bad_gift] I think I'd like to keep looking. //HOW DO??
    Owner: Of course, of course! What can I show you next?
    {$name}: Do you have anything related to Gold Roger?
    <<jump Garp_Gift_Hunt_bad_gift>>
